WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.977
Workflows let your contact center and CRM react to what happens, with no code.

00:00:06.977 --> 00:00:13.310
This video builds one, then tours every task, the CRM event and task, and the runs.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.904
A contact center produces moments that need follow-up:

00:00:21.904 --> 00:00:27.495
a call nobody answered, a dialer attempt that rang out, a lead that qualifies.

00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:29.758
A workflow handles each one:

00:00:29.758 --> 00:00:34.950
an event starts it, tasks do the work, and outcomes decide what is next.

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:40.963
Open Design, Workflows.

00:00:40.963 --> 00:00:43.943
The list shows every workflow on the site.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.862
To make a new one, click Create Workflow.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:51.101
Name it for what it does, here Text customers the dialer could not

00:00:51.101 --> 00:00:52.573
reach, and click Save.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:01:02.158
Add Event adds what starts the workflow, and Add Task adds a step.

00:01:02.158 --> 00:01:05.152
These modules add two event categories:

00:01:05.152 --> 00:01:07.947
Contact Center, and Omnichannel CRM.

00:01:12.139 --> 00:01:14.398
Add the Contact Center Event.

00:01:14.398 --> 00:01:16.722
Its one setting is Event type:

00:01:16.722 --> 00:01:21.239
leave Any event type to react to everything, or choose one kind.

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:23.653
The list is grouped:

00:01:23.653 --> 00:01:32.336
Interaction, Activity, Routing and queues, Agent, Offer, Dialer, Callback, Call, Shared voicemail, Recording,

00:01:32.336 --> 00:01:35.129
Supervision and Secure capture.

00:01:35.592 --> 00:01:42.636
Pick Dialer attempt completed, which fires after every call the dialer places, answered or not.

00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:43.822
Click Save.

00:01:44.274 --> 00:01:46.283
The event has two outcomes.

00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:50.424
Matched is the type you chose, and Ignored is any other event.

00:01:50.424 --> 00:01:53.104
Connect the tasks you want to Matched.

00:01:54.704 --> 00:01:57.421
The event hands the workflow its details:

00:01:57.421 --> 00:02:01.814
the kind of event, the call or conversation, who acted, the agent, and

00:02:01.814 --> 00:02:05.110
its own data, such as the number the dialer called.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.844
Liquid fields read them.

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:12.477
Click Add Task.

00:02:12.477 --> 00:02:15.267
Under Contact Center there are ten.

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:22.764
Enqueue Activity, Find Agent Numbers, Schedule Callback, Schedule Dialer Retry, Send Text Message,

00:02:22.764 --> 00:02:28.480
Set Agent Presence, Start Call Recording, Place Call or Send Message, Stop Call

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.439
Recording, and Hand Off to Live Agent.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.723
Add Send Text Message.

00:02:34.723 --> 00:02:37.292
From is one of your own text numbers.

00:02:37.292 --> 00:02:42.550
To is the customer's number, and a placeholder reads the number the dialer called.

00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:47.112
Message is the text.

00:02:47.112 --> 00:02:48.694
Agent is optional:

00:02:48.694 --> 00:02:53.376
name one so the customer's reply reaches them, or leave it empty.

00:02:53.376 --> 00:02:54.497
Click Save.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:59.348
Drag from the Matched outcome of the event to the task, and save.

00:02:59.348 --> 00:03:03.750
This workflow reacts to dialer calls, so it needs a real phone provider,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.951
and never runs on this demo site.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.348
Place Call or Send Message starts an automated activity now:

00:03:14.348 --> 00:03:19.169
a phone activity is dialed, a text activity is sent its first message.

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:21.580
The one setting is the Activity.

00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:27.127
Set Agent Presence puts an agent into a Status such as Available or Break.

00:03:27.127 --> 00:03:32.721
The reserved, busy and wrap-up states are missing, because the platform sets them.

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:37.707
Find Agent Numbers looks up the numbers an agent calls and texts from.

00:03:37.707 --> 00:03:40.799
Leave User name empty for the default numbers.

00:03:41.251 --> 00:03:46.584
Enqueue Activity puts an activity on a queue so routing can pick an agent.

00:03:46.584 --> 00:03:51.451
Priority keeps the queue's default, or runs from Lowest to Highest.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:56.336
Hand Off to Live Agent moves an automated conversation to people.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:04:00.271
Reason and Summary tell the agent why, and what was said.

00:04:00.271 --> 00:04:03.081
An empty Queue uses the subject flow's.

00:04:03.532 --> 00:04:07.731
Schedule Callback books a callback to a Destination number.

00:04:07.731 --> 00:04:10.767
A Delay of zero minutes makes it due now.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.512
The rest is optional.

00:04:12.962 --> 00:04:17.422
Schedule Dialer Retry makes the dialer call a contact again.

00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:22.152
An empty Delay in minutes uses the dialer profile's retry delay.

00:04:22.605 --> 00:04:27.765
Start Call Recording and Stop Call Recording each take the Interaction to act on.

00:04:31.969 --> 00:04:36.434
The CRM adds one event and one task, under Omnichannel CRM.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:41.449
Lead Converted starts a workflow whenever a lead becomes a contact.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:47.093
Convert Lead converts a lead, for example when a web form says it qualified.

00:04:47.093 --> 00:04:53.680
Account, Create an opportunity, Opportunity type and Other open activities decide what it creates.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.931
Every task ends in an outcome you wire to the next task.

00:05:01.931 --> 00:05:06.897
Place Call or Send Message ends in Done, Already Started or Failed, so

00:05:06.897 --> 00:05:09.380
it never calls a customer twice.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.894
Most tasks end in Done or Failed.

00:05:12.894 --> 00:05:15.658
Find Agent Numbers adds NotFound.

00:05:15.658 --> 00:05:22.390
Hand Off to Live Agent ends in Connected, Waiting In Queue, Callback Scheduled or Failed.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:27.753
Schedule Dialer Retry ends in Scheduled, Exhausted or Failed.

00:05:27.753 --> 00:05:33.124
Call recording can end in Indeterminate, when the change is unconfirmed.

00:05:33.124 --> 00:05:36.360
Convert Lead ends in Converted or Failed.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.369
A workflow this site can run is Look up agent numbers.

00:05:44.369 --> 00:05:48.940
It starts on Agent presence changed, then runs Find Agent Numbers.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:53.174
To raise that event, change presence in the soft phone:

00:05:53.174 --> 00:05:57.330
open the phone, open the presence menu, and choose Available.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.343
Instances lists every run with its status and time.

00:06:01.343 --> 00:06:05.970
Every contact center event starts a run, and one for another kind of

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.720
event ends at Ignored.

00:06:08.171 --> 00:06:11.594
Open a run to see its path through the workflow.

00:06:11.594 --> 00:06:14.828
Restart runs it again, and Delete removes it.

00:06:14.828 --> 00:06:18.061
Settings, Workflow Trimming removes old runs.

00:06:22.261 --> 00:06:23.794
Record every call:

00:06:23.794 --> 00:06:27.436
start on Call connected, then Start Call Recording.

00:06:27.436 --> 00:06:29.545
Follow up on a missed call:

00:06:29.545 --> 00:06:33.251
start on Dialer attempt completed, then send a text.

00:06:34.001 --> 00:06:38.483
Escalate an automated conversation with Hand Off to Live Agent.

00:06:38.483 --> 00:06:42.901
Welcome a new customer with Convert Lead, then Lead Converted.

00:06:43.651 --> 00:06:48.463
A workflow cannot transfer a live call or pick a particular agent.

00:06:48.463 --> 00:06:51.671
Use Enqueue Activity, and routing chooses.

00:06:53.671 --> 00:06:59.459
Events start the workflow, tasks do the work, and outcomes decide what happens next.

00:06:59.459 --> 00:07:01.131
Thanks for watching.

